  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This survey reviews five quantum machine learning anomaly-detection case studies including IoMT security (accuracy up to 99.34%), hybrid deep anomaly detection on MNIST/Fashion-MNIST (AUC up to 89.41%), a 4‑qubit hybrid quantum autoencoder for power-plant sensor data (64.1% recall), QCNN-based surveillance anomaly detection (accuracy up to 1.00 in some class settings), and a quantum-kernel fraud detector (~70% average precision). All experiments rely on small circuits or simulators and do not demonstrate computational quantum advantage.",
